Mr. Penhaligon,<br />
<br />
The staff's deficiency letter arising from examination 2011-0447 is attache=
d. It describes six deficiencies and requires Marchwood to implement correc=
tive action for each.<br />
<br />
Item 4 concerns custody. The staff's position is that Marchwood's standing =
authority to instruct client custodians to debit advisory fees constitutes =
custody of client funds within the meaning of Rule 206(4)-2 under the Inves=
tment Advisers Act, that Marchwood was therefore required to obtain a surpr=
ise examination by an independent public accountant for calendar year 2010,=
 and that no such examination was obtained and no Form ADV-E was filed.<br =
/>
<br />
Please respond in writing within 30 days describing the corrective action M=
archwood will take on each of the six items. As the letter states, the abov=
e findings are based on the staff's examination and are not findings or con=
clusions of the Commission.<br />
<br />
Rosalind Achterberg<br />
Branch Chief, Investment Adviser / Investment Company Examinations<br />
Philadelphia Regional Office
